<title>FRANCE: Bouygues Offshore plans 3 Ffr 96 gross div.</title>
<headline>Bouygues Offshore plans 3 Ffr 96 gross div.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bouygues Offshore, which plans to float 40 percent of its capital on the French and U.S. stock markets, expects to pay a 1996 gross dividend of three francs per share, the company's finance director Philippe Marien told a news conference on Thursday.</p>
<p>Bouygues Offshore, an international contractor serving the oil and gas industry, expected 1996 net attributable profit to be stable or slightly below the 171 million francs it posted for 1995, he said.</p>
<p>Bouygues Offshore, a unit of French construction company Bouygues SA, has said it plans to be floated on the French and U.S. stock markets in November.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
